{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.barOdd_div_qPowOdd_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.barOdd_div_qPowOdd_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L262-L268","doc":"**The answer to `qou-fi93`'s residual.**  Any bar-odd function agrees\nwith `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ` up to a bar-even factor, wherever the latter is nonzero —\nbecause both are the same generator times a bar-even function.  So `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ`\nis not selected: it is representative of the whole channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd_eq_skein_mul_qIntSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd_eq_skein_mul_qIntSym","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L253-L260","doc":"`qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ = (q − q⁻¹)·[n]_q`, holding at the fixed points of the bar too\n(both sides vanish there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_eq_qPowOdd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_eq_qPowOdd_one","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L248-L251","doc":"The generator is the `n = 1` member of its own family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qIntSym_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qIntSym_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L243-L246","doc":"`[n]_q` is bar-even, and the proof is the mechanism rather than a\ncomputation: it is a ratio of two bar-odd objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L238-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qIntSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qIntSym","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L235-L236","doc":"The symmetric q-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.qPowOdd","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L232-L233","doc":"The undivided object `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.isBarOdd_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.isBarOdd_iff","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L208-L228","doc":"**The bar-odd channel is free of rank one over the bar-even part**, with\nthe skein coefficient `q − q⁻¹` as generator.\n\nA function is bar-odd **iff** it is the generator times a bar-even function.\nSo there is no *choice* of bar-odd object: every one factors through the same\n`q − q⁻¹`.  This is what turns `qou-fi93`'s `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ` from an exhibited\ncandidate into the only shape available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L197-L204","doc":"The generator vanishes exactly at the fixed points of the bar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.eq_zero_of_inv_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.eq_zero_of_inv_self","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L185-L195","doc":"A bar-odd function vanishes wherever the bar has a fixed point, i.e. at\n`q⁻¹ = q` (`q² = 1`).  This is the only place the characteristic enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L174-L181","doc":"Multiplying any bar-even function by the generator lands in the bar-odd\npart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.div_skein_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.div_skein_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L166-L172","doc":"Dividing any bar-odd function by the generator lands in the bar-even\npart.  No hypothesis on `q² ≠ 1` is needed: where the generator vanishes the\nbar has a fixed point, so both sides of the bar-even equation are literally\nthe same expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.div_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.div_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L158-L164","doc":"**The mechanism `qou-fi93` measured.**  A ratio of two bar-odd functions\nis bar-even — the two sign flips cancel.  This is *why* `[n]_q =\n(qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)` carries no bar-odd content: not an absence of\nstructure, but the same factor divided out twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven.mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven.mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L154-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd.mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L150-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven.mul","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L146-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L138-L142","doc":"The generator is itself bar-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.skein","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L133-L136","doc":"The **skein coefficient** `q − q⁻¹`: the Hecke structure constant in\n`σᵢ² = (q − q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1`, equivalently the coefficient in the skein relation\n`L₊ − L₋ = (q − q⁻¹)L₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarOdd","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L129-L131","doc":"A function of the modulus is **bar-odd** when the bar involution negates\nit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BarParityRankOne.IsBarEven","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/BarParityRankOne.lean#L125-L127","doc":"A function of the modulus is **bar-even** when the bar involution\n`q ↦ q⁻¹` leaves it unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}